title": "Stephen Wolfram", "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/broadcasts/2OdXkLbYqkXQjX", "url": "https://t.co/QbjyiVyIHq"}]}, "id": "2118079564446380307", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 1612, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "History of Science and Technology Q&amp;A [Wolfram Tech Edition] (November 4, 2026) https://t.co/QbjyiVyIHq", "url": "https://x.com/stephen_wolfram/status/2118079564446380307"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:25:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118077105611129129"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - Researchers hope that US lawmakers will push back against the Trump administration’s science policies — but there are limits to what Congress can do.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/4iw9Sib", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/4iw9Sib", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118077110761709569/g7q-VPkg?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118077110761709569/g7q-VPkg?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 219, "status": 200, "title": "‘Historic change’: what the 2026 US mid-term election results mean for science", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03579-x?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64320533&error=cookies_not_supported&code=14ac8c21-598e-4890-b70e-01e8220b6727", "url": "https://t.co/LKYRUboDcz"}]}, "id": "2118077105611129129", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3528, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "The US mid-term elections swept the Democratic party to power in both chambers of the US Congress, raising hopes that lawmakers will now push back against disruptions to science introduced by the Trump administration.\n\nhttps://t.co/LKYRUboDcz", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2118077105611129129"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:06:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118072359013753026"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 42, "start": 27, "tag": "SciencePodcast"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/4jk2JbOTwz", "end": 288, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2118072359013753026/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118072294694125568", "start": 265, "url": "https://t.co/4jk2JbOTwz"}]}, "id": "2118072359013753026", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5276, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "In the last episode of the #SciencePodcast🎙️ series on scientific biographies, Joseph Osmundson explores how queer parenthood intersects with themes present throughout the natural world, evoking questions about community and identity along the way.\n\n🎧 Listen here: https://t.co/4jk2JbOTwz", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2118072359013753026"}, {"author_id": "407985006", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:03:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118071543137726907"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Metals typically rely on electrons to transport heat, but one has been identified that conducts heat efficiently through both electrons and phonons.", "display_url": "go.aps.org/4zxS4uC", "end": 238, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/4zxS4uC", "images": [{"height": 250, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118071550456832000/P9Bu5qFi?format=png&name=orig", "width": 500}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118071550456832000/P9Bu5qFi?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 215, "status": 200, "title": "A Metal with Two Heat Carriers", "unwound_url": "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v19/s136", "url": "https://t.co/aOnBMMcrpy"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/LgGQKCEWCB", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2118071543137726907/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118071540574990336", "start": 239, "url": "https://t.co/LgGQKCEWCB"}]}, "id": "2118071543137726907", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 252, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "While metals typically rely on electrons to transport heat, researchers have now identified a specific crystal form of tantalum nitride that conducts heat efficiently through both electrons and phonons.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/aOnBMMcrpy https://t.co/LgGQKCEWCB", "url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2118071543137726907"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-04T19:56:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118069842787889603"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The clinicians and researchers who will take office are ready to tackle the U.S. health care system.", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/04/mid…", "end": 135, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/04/midterms-democrat-winners-doctors-scientists-medical-professionals/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118053605903122433/i6-cwYDo?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118053605903122433/i6-cwYDo?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 112, "status": 200, "title": "Democratic doctors and scientists ride the blue wave", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/04/midterms-democrat-winners-doctors-scientists-medical-professionals/", "url": "https://t.co/oxhb8sgO9t"}]}, "id": "2118069842787889603", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 961, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Democratic doctors and scientists ride the blue wave. Here’s how their backgrounds may influence health policy. https://t.co/oxhb8sgO9t", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2118069842787889603"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-04T19:49:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118068101627433088"